{
  "$comment": [
    "Verified npm registry facts for the libraries the agents make version claims",
    "about. Used by scripts/test.mjs to reject version numbers that were never",
    "published.",
    "",
    "Why this exists: the animation agent asserted that 'Reanimated 4.7.x supports",
    "RN 0.85-0.87 and wants worklets 0.13.x'. There is no 4.7.x release — 4.7.0",
    "exists only as a nightly dist-tag. The real latest, 4.6.0, declares",
    "react-native '0.83 - 0.87' and worklets '0.12.x'. The fabricated numbers were",
    "in four places at once, including the `why` text of the FORBIDDEN_ABSOLUTES",
    "guard written to prevent version fabrication, and a test fixture asserting it.",
    "A wrong version is worse than a vague one: it is specific enough to be acted",
    "on and wrong enough to waste an afternoon.",
    "",
    "Rule: a released version listed here must exist on the registry. Do not add a",
    "number to make a failure go away."
  ],
